---
description: Spontus backend implementation guidance
alwaysApply: true
---

Read docs/engineering/backend-plan.md before implementing auth, database, storage, API routes, server actions, or data fetching.

Backend rules:
- Use Supabase-ready data structures unless the team explicitly chooses another backend.
- Use Team + Sponsor as the core account sides.
- Use Brand only as sponsor display identity.
- Keep the sponsorship asset taxonomy shared between team profiles and sponsor listings.
- Keep manual verification status in the MVP.
- Enable Row Level Security on all app tables once Supabase tables exist.
- Do not rely on frontend-only access checks for sensitive data.
- Keep mock data shaped like future database rows.

First backend slice:
- profiles
- teams
- team_memberships
- team_profiles
- team_events
- sponsorship_asset_definitions
- team_sponsorship_assets

Do not build these in the first backend slice unless explicitly requested:
- payments
- escrow
- tax workflows
- AI contracts
- automated matching
- advanced analytics
- full CRM
- social API ingestion
- youth sports compliance engine

When adding backend code:
1. Identify which MVP slice the backend work belongs to.
2. Link the change to docs/engineering/backend-plan.md.
3. Keep migrations small and reversible.
4. Add seed data for canonical sponsorship assets when relevant.
5. Summarize RLS assumptions and any security gaps after implementation.
